## Evidence
`/dev/shm/zlink-tmp-node/zlink-zoneworld-I8r3Nz/logs/gateway.log` (lines 7-24: the ConfigError and stack), gate log
`/tmp/claude-1000/-home-hep7-project-zlink/be443aad-d720-4c23-9860-099f913fdfd4/scratchpad/gate13-node-samples.log`.

## Fix (single owner)
In the STREAM session service owner (`packages/framework/src/runtime/backend/node/node-raw-mesh-backend.ts` deliver path and any other `disconnect_rid`/session-close call
sites): "closing a session that Core no longer has" is a completed close (idempotent) — map the binding's NOT_FOUND result to the session-closed outcome at that owner, no
catch-all, and the session's local state is cleaned exactly as for a normal close. Any other disconnect_rid failure stays an error with its typed kind. Regression test:
deliver to a bound session whose RID Core already dropped → no throw, session closed once, ingress pump continues. Also check dotnet/java equivalents (`ZLinkBoundSessionService`,
`ZLinkJavaStreamSocket` close paths) for the same NOT_FOUND handling and state parity (report; do not change other languages).

## Verify
`stream-runtime`, `stream-session-runtime`, `raw-service-mesh` contract tests; ZoneWorld ×3 (exit 0, all verdicts); `bash samples/run_samples.sh` once; `npm test` once (report
`stream-actor-bind-replay.test.js` separately if it fails — it is under the Core investigation).

